---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { cases, steps, dont, embeddedKicker, updatedLabel } from '../lib/data';

const path = '/embedded-ai-delivery';
const updated = updatedLabel(path);
---
<Base path={path}>
<div>
<div style="padding:clamp(48px,7vw,80px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px) clamp(40px,5vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14)">
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:30px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.2em;color:#8a5a3c">{embeddedKicker}</div><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:#5c5d51">LAST UPDATED {updated}</div></div>
<h1 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(38px,5.4vw,72px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.025em;max-width:18ch;text-wrap:balance">We don't write you a strategy. We come in and <em style="color:#8a5a3c">build it with your team</em>.</h1>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px;margin-top:40px;align-items:flex-start">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33;max-width:700px;text-wrap:pretty">Twelve years of shipping software for businesses that could not afford it to go wrong, now pointed at one thing: getting AI into the operating fabric of mid-market and PE-backed companies. I lead every engagement personally, with a small bench of senior engineers and designers brought in as the work needs. Internal tooling, automation and agents, in production, owned by your people.</p>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 22px;align-items:center;align-self:stretch">
<a href="/contact" style="flex:none;white-space:nowrap;text-decoration:none;background:#15160f;color:#f5f2ea;padding:14px 24px;min-height:48px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;font-size:15px;font-weight:500">Book 30 minutes</a>
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:#5c5d51">FREE · UNDER AN HOUR · STRAIGHT ANSWER ON FIT</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="padding:clamp(46px,6vw,70px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14)">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-.02em">Four ways in</h2>
<p style="margin:0 0 36px;font-size:16px;color:#5c5d51;max-width:620px">Most engagements start with the first and grow into the others. All fixed price against a defined outcome.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:1px;background:transparent;border:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);--cell:1">
<div style="background:#f5f2ea;outline:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);padding:34px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#8a5a3c">01 · EMBEDDED SPRINT</div><h3 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.15">Two to three weeks inside the business</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">We sit with the people doing the work — ops, finance, sales, support — and map where the hours and the errors actually go. By the end of the sprint the top one or two are automated and running, not specified.</p><div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);font-size:14px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.6">You leave with: working software, a ranked and costed backlog, and a team that has watched it be built.</div></div>
<div style="background:#f5f2ea;outline:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);padding:34px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#8a5a3c">02 · INTERNAL TOOLING</div><h3 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.15">The software the roadmap keeps deferring</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">Every business has three internal tools it has wanted for two years — the pricing calculator, the ops dashboard, the thing that kills the spreadsheet. Built properly on your stack, with AI where it earns its place.</p><div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);font-size:14px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.6">You leave with: production software, documentation, and engineers able to extend it.</div></div>
<div style="background:#f5f2ea;outline:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);padding:34px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#8a5a3c">03 · AUTOMATION &amp; AGENTS</div><h3 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.15">Cost out of the operation, permanently</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">Quoting, onboarding, reconciliation, reporting, support triage, document handling. Agents built against your systems and your data, with a human in the loop wherever judgement or liability sits.</p><div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);font-size:14px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.6">You leave with: a measured before-and-after on hours, cost and error rate.</div></div>
<div style="background:#f5f2ea;outline:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);padding:34px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#8a5a3c">04 · CAPABILITY TRANSFER</div><h3 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.15">Your team, AI-native for real</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">You bought the licences and nothing changed. We work alongside your engineers and operators until the workflows they use daily are the ones with AI in them — then deliberately make ourselves unnecessary.</p><div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);font-size:14px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.6">You leave with: habits and workflows that survive our departure. Measured at six months.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="padding:clamp(46px,6vw,70px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);background:#eeeade;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:clamp(28px,4vw,60px)">
<div style="max-width:320px"><h2 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.1">How an engagement runs</h2><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#5c5d51">No rate card, no juniors, no hand-off once the pitch is won. If we finish faster we earn a better margin; if we underestimate, we absorb it.</p></div>
<div style="grid-column:span 2;min-width:0">
{steps.map((s) => (<Fragment>
<div class="r-step" style="display:grid;gap:20px;padding:24px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.18);align-items:start"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8a5a3c">{s.n}</span><div><div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;margin-bottom:6px">{s.title}</div><div style="font-size:15.5px;color:#3c3d33;line-height:1.6">{s.body}</div></div><span class="r-time" style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:#5c5d51;letter-spacing:.1em">{s.time}</span></div>
</Fragment>))}
</div>
</div>

<div style="padding:clamp(46px,6vw,70px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:clamp(28px,4vw,60px)">
<div style="max-width:320px"><div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#8a5a3c;margin-bottom:12px">THE ANTI-OFFER</div><h2 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.1">What we don't do</h2><p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#5c5d51">Saying no to these is most of what makes the rest work.</p></div>
<div style="grid-column:span 2;min-width:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:0 36px">
{dont.map((d) => (<Fragment>
<div style="padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);display:grid;grid-template-columns:22px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;align-items:start"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;color:#8a5a3c;line-height:1.4">×</span><div><div style="font-size:16.5px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:3px">{d.t}</div><div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#3c3d33">{d.b}</div></div></div>
</Fragment>))}
</div>
</div>
<div style="padding:clamp(46px,6vw,70px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14)">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 30px;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-.02em">Recent work</h2>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:24px">
{cases.map((c) => (<Fragment>
<div style="border:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.16);padding:30px 28px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#8a5a3c">{c.tag}</div>
<h3 style="margin:0;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:24px;line-height:1.18">{c.title}</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#3c3d33">{c.body}</p>
<div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-size:30px;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.02em">{c.stat1}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.4">{c.label1}</div></div>
<div><div style="font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-size:30px;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.02em">{c.stat2}</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#5c5d51;line-height:1.4">{c.label2}</div></div>
</div>
</div>
</Fragment>))}
</div>
</div>

<div style="padding:clamp(46px,6vw,70px) clamp(20px,4vw,60px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(21,22,15,.14)">
<h2 style="margin:0 0 32px;font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-.02em">Why this isn't a consultancy</h2>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:34px">
<div style="border-top:2px solid #8a5a3c;padding-top:18px"><h3 style="margin:0 0 9px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">Senior hands, small bench</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">Brannan leads every engagement and does the work. Where it needs more hands, senior engineers and designers he's shipped with for a decade — never a pyramid with his face on the pitch.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid rgba(21,22,15,.25);padding-top:18px"><h3 style="margin:0 0 9px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">Priced on outcome</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">Fixed against a defined result, agreed before we start. Same side of the table about speed.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid rgba(21,22,15,.25);padding-top:18px"><h3 style="margin:0 0 9px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">Built to be left behind</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">Your stack, your repos, your accounts. Nothing depends on us after handover — that's the test the work is held to.</p></div>
<div style="border-top:2px solid rgba(21,22,15,.25);padding-top:18px"><h3 style="margin:0 0 9px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">We'll tell you when not to</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#3c3d33">A good proportion of AI ideas are worse than fixing the process. No incentive to pretend otherwise; we'll say so on the first call.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</Base>
